// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// boot.slint — what the machine is actually doing, while it does it
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// The old one was a seven-second animation: embers drifted, converged, an orb kindled, text
// faded, and then it handed over. Four phases on a timer, and a status line that said
// "remembering..." for the whole of it. None of it was connected to anything. The machine was
// starting nine services, loading an embedder, opening a database and waking a companion, and
// the screen in front of the person said nothing about any of it — the first thing anybody sees
// of this OS was a screensaver with a progress-shaped animation on top.
//
// So the stages here are real. Each one is a thing the shell genuinely waits for, and its state
// comes from whether that thing has happened. When the companion is slow because it is fetching
// an embedder, the line about memory sits at "working" and says so. That is the same rule the
// agent rail lives by, applied to the one screen where a person has nothing to do but read.
//
// # Why it looks like the desktop
//
// The same scene wallpaper, dimmed. Boot is not a separate place the machine passes through on
// the way to being itself; it is the machine, earlier. Arriving at the desktop should feel like
// the lights coming up, not like a different program starting.

import { Theme } from "theme.slint";
import { Icon, Icons } from "components/icon.slint";
import { YantrikMark, YantrikName } from "components/yantrik_mark.slint";

export struct BootStage {
    label: string,
    // What it is doing right now. Shown only while this stage is the one running.
    detail: string,
    // 0 pending, 1 running, 2 done
    state: int,
}

component StageRow inherits HorizontalLayout {
    in property <BootStage> stage;

    spacing: Theme.sp-3;
    height: 34px;

    // ── The mark ──
    //
    // Three states, three shapes: an empty ring for what has not started, a bright ring for
    // what is happening, a filled tick for what is finished. Readable without the words.
    Rectangle {
        width: 20px;
        height: 20px;
        y: (parent.height - 20px) / 2;
        border-radius: 10px;
        background: root.stage.state == 2 ? Theme.accent : transparent;
        border-width: root.stage.state == 2 ? 0px : 2px;
        border-color: root.stage.state == 1 ? Theme.accent : Theme.border-strong;

        if root.stage.state == 2 : Icon {
            commands: Icons.check;
            size: 20px;
            thickness: 2px;
            tint: Theme.text-on-accent;
            x: (parent.width - self.width) / 2;
            y: (parent.height - self.height) / 2;
        }
    }

    VerticalLayout {
        alignment: center;
        spacing: 1px;
        horizontal-stretch: 1;

        Text {
            text: root.stage.label;
            color: root.stage.state == 0 ? Theme.text-dim : Theme.text-primary;
            font-size: Theme.fs-body;
            font-weight: root.stage.state == 1 ? 600 : 400;
        }
        // Only the running stage explains itself. A list where every line has a subtitle is a
        // list nobody reads.
        if root.stage.state == 1 && root.stage.detail != "" : Text {
            text: root.stage.detail;
            color: Theme.text-dim;
            font-size: Theme.fs-micro;
            overflow: elide;
        }
    }

    Text {
        text: root.stage.state == 2 ? "Done" : "";
        color: Theme.text-dim;
        font-size: Theme.fs-caption;
        vertical-alignment: center;
    }
}

export component BootScreen inherits Rectangle {
    in property <string> status-text: "";
    in property <int> memory-count: 0;
    in property <[BootStage]> stages: [];
    // 0..1. Driven by the stages, not by a clock.
    in property <float> progress: 0.0;
    in property <string> version: "";
    in property <int> ambient-interval-ms: 0;
    callback boot-complete();

    background: Theme.bg-deep;
    clip: true;

    // ── The scene, dimmed ──
    Image {
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
        source: @image-url("wallpapers/serenity.png");
        image-fit: fill;
        opacity: 0.45;
    }
    // A wash over it, so white text on the horizon stays readable wherever the ridge falls.
    Rectangle {
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
        background: @linear-gradient(180deg,
            Theme.bg-deep.transparentize(30%) 0%,
            Theme.bg-deep.transparentize(55%) 45%,
            Theme.bg-deep.transparentize(25%) 100%);
    }

    // ── Corners ──
    //
    // The quiet furniture of a product that knows what it is. Four short lines, none of them
    // competing with the middle.
    Text {
        x: 40px;
        y: 40px;
        text: "BUILT\nFOR A MORE\nCAPABLE YOU";
        color: Theme.text-dim;
        font-size: Theme.fs-micro;
        letter-spacing: 1.5px;
    }
    HorizontalLayout {
        x: parent.width - self.preferred-width - 40px;
        y: 40px;
        // With no height this layout filled the screen, and the 1px rule below — centred in its
        // parent — landed halfway down the boot screen as a stray dash floating over the
        // mountains. An absolutely-positioned layout has to be given both.
        height: 14px;
        spacing: Theme.sp-3;
        Rectangle {
            width: 18px;
            height: 1px;
            y: (parent.height - 1px) / 2;
            background: Theme.text-dim;
        }
        Text {
            text: "A MORE CAPABLE TOMORROW";
            color: Theme.text-dim;
            font-size: Theme.fs-micro;
            letter-spacing: 1.5px;
        }
    }
    Text {
        x: 40px;
        y: parent.height - 40px - self.preferred-height;
        text: "Yantrik OS   " + root.version;
        color: Theme.text-dim;
        font-size: Theme.fs-micro;
    }
    Text {
        x: parent.width - self.preferred-width - 40px;
        y: parent.height - 40px - self.preferred-height;
        text: "PRIVATE  /  LOCAL  /  MORE CAPABLE";
        color: Theme.text-dim;
        font-size: Theme.fs-micro;
        letter-spacing: 1.5px;
    }

    // ── The middle ──
    VerticalLayout {
        x: (parent.width - 520px) / 2;
        width: 520px;
        y: 76px;
        height: parent.height - 152px;
        alignment: start;
        spacing: 0;

        HorizontalLayout {
            alignment: center;
            YantrikMark {
                mark-size: 132px;
            }
        }

        Rectangle { height: Theme.sp-5; }

        // The name, as the brand sets it (brand/yantrik-name.svg): the stacked lockup.
        HorizontalLayout {
            alignment: center;
            YantrikName { cap-height: 30px; }
        }
        Rectangle { height: Theme.sp-3; }
        HorizontalLayout {
            alignment: center;
            Text {
                text: "Your computer. More capable.";
                color: Theme.text-secondary;
                font-size: Theme.fs-title-2;
            }
        }

        Rectangle { height: Theme.sp-6; }

        // ── Progress ──
        HorizontalLayout {
            spacing: Theme.sp-4;
            height: 8px;

            Rectangle {
                horizontal-stretch: 1;
                height: 6px;
                y: (parent.height - 6px) / 2;
                border-radius: 3px;
                background: Theme.bg-deep.transparentize(35%);
                border-width: 1px;
                border-color: Theme.glass-border;

                Rectangle {
                    x: 0;
                    width: parent.width * root.progress;
                    height: 100%;
                    border-radius: 3px;
                    background: Theme.accent;
                    animate width { duration: 400ms; easing: ease-out; }
                }
            }
            Text {
                text: Math.round(root.progress * 100) + "%";
                color: Theme.text-secondary;
                font-size: Theme.fs-caption;
                vertical-alignment: center;
                min-width: 40px;
            }
        }

        Rectangle { height: Theme.sp-5; }

        // ── What is happening ──
        VerticalLayout {
            spacing: Theme.sp-2;
            for s in root.stages : StageRow { stage: s; }
        }

        Rectangle { vertical-stretch: 1; }

        Rectangle { height: 1px; background: Theme.separator; }
        Rectangle { height: Theme.sp-4; }

        HorizontalLayout {
            alignment: center;
            spacing: Theme.sp-2;
            Icon {
                commands: Icons.lock;
                size: 14px;
                tint: Theme.text-dim;
                y: (parent.height - self.height) / 2;
            }
            Text {
                text: "Local-first. Private by default.";
                color: Theme.text-secondary;
                font-size: Theme.fs-caption;
                vertical-alignment: center;
            }
        }
        Rectangle { height: Theme.sp-2; }
        HorizontalLayout {
            alignment: center;
            Text {
                // The one line that changes with the machine's own words.
                text: root.status-text != ""
                    ? root.status-text
                    : "Please wait while Yantrik gets things ready.";
                color: Theme.text-dim;
                font-size: Theme.fs-caption;
            }
        }
    }
}
